                "<div class=\"detailed-body\">\n"
                "<p><strong>Alan Marshall's Taxonomy of Environmental Thought:</strong> Environmental philosopher Alan Marshall formulated a postmodern framework capturing how human ethical relationships with nature have evolved over the last four decades. He categorized these emerging ethics into three distinct streams: (1) Libertarian Extension, (2) Ecologic Extension, and (3) Conservation Ethics. The first two represent radical departures from anthropocentrism, but they arrive at nature's defense through entirely different pathways—one through political rights, and the other through ecological science.</p>\n"
                "<h4>Structured Comparison Matrix</h4>\n"
