                "<li><strong>Libertarian Extension (A Political Reflection):</strong>\n"
                "<p>Libertarian Extension borrows directly from political philosophy, particularly the historical movements that extended civil liberties—first from monarchs to landowners, then to all men, then to women, and across racial minorities. Libertarian extension argues that the natural next step in moral progress is extending equal rights to non-human members of our planetary community. It asserts that animals and living organisms possess basic rights to life, freedom from torture, and the ability to fulfill their natural lives. As detailed in Slide 14, Deep Ecology's fundamental argument—that nature possesses intrinsic value and inherent worth—firmly falls under Libertarian Extension. Because it mirrors political emancipation, it can be viewed as a <em>political reflection of the natural world</em>.</p></li>\n"
