                "<div class=\"detailed-body\">\n"
                "<p><strong>The Legislative Timeline of Indian Environmental Governance:</strong> The legal framework governing the environment in India was built chronologically through specific parliamentary acts addressing emerging industrial crises, global treaties, and supreme judicial interventions. The 5-mark match matrix from End Exam 2022 tests this core statutory timeline.</p>\n"
                "<h4>Structured Chronological Match Table</h4>\n"
                "<table class=\"exam-table\">\n"
                "<thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>Statute / Rule</th><th>Constitutional / Historical Trigger</th><th>Core Regulatory Mandate</th></tr></thead>\n"
                "<tbody>\n"
                "<tr><td><strong>1972</strong></td><td><strong>The Wildlife (Protection) Act</strong></td><td>Rapid decline of megafauna (tiger, elephant) and uncontrolled commercial poaching.</td><td>Created National Parks, Sanctuaries, 6 protection schedules; total ban on hunting.</td></tr>\n"
